  "editorialSummary": "Nothing says peak efficiency quite like crypto exchanges losing billions to [fake job interviews](https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/nx-s1-6027799/binance-crypto-exchange-cyber-heist) while German automotive giants [axe thousands of jobs](https://www.ft.com/content/25ce0d50-e7b6-4b14-93bb-ee5da6f747c0?syn-25a6b1a6=1) and Washington ponders [strikes on Qeshm Island](https://www.latercera.com/mundo/noticia/en-medio-de-las-midterms-estados-unidos-ataca-la-isla-qeshm-en-ormuz/). At least paleontologists extracting [red blood cells from dinosaur fossils](https://www.newscientist.com/article/2596881-dinosaur-red-blood-cells-recovered-from-115-million-year-old-fossil/?utm_campaign=RSS|NSNS&utm_content=home&utm_medium=RSS&utm_source=NSNS) finally have some fresh management material to study.",
